TITLE:: RLTimePoints
summary:: Time points and the pulses between them: the context of metre networks
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLPulse, Classes/RLTimeMap, Classes/RLNetwork, Classes/RLMetre, Classes/RLTimeSpans, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
A time point is a number (a time in bars, in beats, in seconds). The arrows are pulses (link::Classes/RLPulse::): M(d) relates two points a whole number of d apart. A metre network (Popoff and Yust) is an link::Classes/RLNetwork:: on this context: its nodes hold time points, its arrows say which pulse joins them, and two routes compose alike.

Networks are carried into one another (link::Classes/RLNetwork#-isMorphismTo::) in the two ways metre has of being at odds with itself: a pulse included in a finer one (a grouping), and a shift of time (a displacement). The maps of time, link::Classes/RLTimeMap::, are the automorphisms.

code::
// Brahms, "Auf dem See" op. 106 no. 2, bars 7 and 8, the bar as the unit
~time = RLTimePoints.new;
~top = RLNetwork(~time, [[\E, 5/2], [\G, 3]], [[\E, \G, 1/2]]);                              // a half bar
~voice = RLNetwork(~time, [[\E, 5/2], [\F, 17/6], [\G, 3]], [[\E, \F, 1/6], [\F, \G, 1/6]]); // the voice: eighths
~top.isMorphismTo(~voice);                               // true: M1/2 is included in M1/6
~piano = RLNetwork(~time, [[\E, 31/12], [\G, 37/12]], [[\E, \G, 1/2]]);                      // the piano, a sixteenth later
~top.isMorphismTo(~piano, nil, ~time.shift(1/12));       // true: a displacement
~fine = RLNetwork(~time, [[\E, 31/12], [\F, 17/6], [\G, 37/12]], [[\E, \F, 'M1/4'], [\F, \G, 'M1/4']]);   // dotted eighths
~piano.isMorphismTo(~fine);                              // true
~voice.morphismProblems(~fine, nil, ~time.shift(1/12));  // what is in the way of eighths against dotted eighths

~time.dissonance([1/6, 5/2], [1/4, 31/12]);              // grouping
~time.common([1/6, 5/2], [1/4, 31/12]);                  // [0.5, 2.8333333333]: they meet every half bar, at 17/6 first
::

A name with a slash is written between quotes: code::'M1/4'::, not code::\M1/4::, which sclang reads as a division.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: arrow
A pulse from what names it: an link::Classes/RLPulse::, a period, a name (code::'M1/6'::, code::"1/6"::), or a word of them (their gcd).

METHOD:: transform
METHOD:: pulse
The same, for one name or one period.

METHOD:: identityTransform
M0.

METHOD:: nameOf
A pulse's name.

METHOD:: affine
METHOD:: shift
METHOD:: stretch
The maps of time code::t -> a t + b:: (link::Classes/RLTimeMap::): both, a shift alone, a stretch alone.

METHOD:: pulseOf
The finest pulse that holds a list of time points: every two of them a whole number of its periods apart.

METHOD:: layer
The points of a pulse layer in a window. A layer is code::[period, phase]::, or a period alone: the points phase + k period.

METHOD:: dissonance
How two pulse layers stand to one another: code::\consonance:: when the points of the slower are all points of the faster; code::\displacement:: when their periods would allow that and they are shifted apart (Krebs); code::\grouping:: when neither period is a whole multiple of the other.

METHOD:: common
The points two layers both sound, as a layer code::[period, one of its points]::: the period is their lcm. nil when they share no point.

METHOD:: system
nil: time points have no pitch system.
